# Multi-agent coordination
#
# Three people, one shared goal, and nobody in charge.
#
# `contribute` is scored like every other action: its pull is the mean trust an
# agent feels toward the rest of its group, plus hope and pride; what holds it
# back is the mean doubt, plus fear, sadness and shame.  So the group makes
# progress at a rate that *is* the state of its relationships -- there is no
# coordination protocol and no task assignment anywhere.
#
# Charlie doubts Alice, and Bob is frightened.  The question the program asks is
# whether a group can still act when its trust graph is broken in two places.
#
# Compare with `coordination_broken.catharsis`, which is the same program with
# the doubt turned up, and never reaches its goal.

group rescue_team

agent alice bob charlie

join alice rescue_team
join bob rescue_team
join charlie rescue_team

goal rescue_team "rescue"

trust alice bob 0.7
trust bob charlie 0.7
trust charlie alice 0.3
doubt charlie alice 0.5

fear bob 0.5
hope alice 0.6
pride charlie 0.5

tick 20

observe rescue_team
observe bob
